<section class="section-padding bg-bg-section dark:bg-bg-section-dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Common questions</p><h2>Before we discuss the website</h2></div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
            <article class="faq-card"><h3>Do you work with small charities?</h3><p>Yes. The useful starting point is the organisation’s needs and decision-making process, not its size. I will recommend a proportionate scope rather than unnecessary features.</p></article>
            <article class="faq-card"><h3>Can trustees review the proposal?</h3><p>Yes. I provide a clear scope, price, responsibilities and service terms that can be shared with decision-makers before work begins.</p></article>
            <article class="faq-card"><h3>Do you guarantee a particular accessibility standard?</h3><p>Accessibility is built into my normal approach, but formal conformance requirements must be agreed in the project scope so the necessary review and testing can be planned properly.</p></article>
            <article class="faq-card"><h3>Can you support the website after launch?</h3><p>Yes. Managed plans include hosting and ongoing care. A one-off build can also have separately agreed hosting or support if your organisation needs it.</p></article>
